------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY  (web source reproduced — Honesty Covenant #2/#5, no narrowing/shortcuts)
------------------------------------------------------------
The web `UsageCard` is a PURE presentational primitive ("no hooks, no API calls, no
derived state. Every dynamic value comes in via props"). Shared by TWO consumers
(TeslaApiUsageCard + AiUsageCard). The native AiUsageCard surface
(TeslaSync/feature-views/AiUsageCard*) already exists and its Views file explicitly
notes the shared atomic peer "is owned by the P4 component-library bundle (out of
scope here, and not yet present)" — THIS prompt delivers that peer.

- Data sources: NONE (pure presentational) — content arrives via `UsageCardContent`,
  the native mirror of `UsageCardProps`. The view is a pure function of that value.
- Shared components used: NONE (atomic primitive) — built from raw SwiftUI + the
  P1/S9 design tokens (Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius). No Tailwind ports,
  no raw hex.
- Charts / maps: NONE.
- Composition reproduced section-for-section (web -> native subview):
    BudgetSection   -> UsageCardBudgetSection   (headline + right caption, clamped
                       progress track, sub-caption; width clamps to 100% while the
                       a11y percent stays UNCLAMPED so over-budget overflow is
                       announced — web `Math.max(0, Math.min(100, pct))` /
                       `Math.max(0, Math.round(pct))` parity).
    BandsSection    -> UsageCardBandsSection     (adaptive 3-col grid; icon + uppercase
                       label, tabular value, sub; intent ring + tint).
    DetailsSection  -> UsageCardDetailsSection   (adaptive 4-col grid; intent value
                       colour).
    TopListsSection -> UsageCardTopListsSection   (adaptive 2-col grid; monospaced
                       label / tabular value rows).
    BannerSection   -> UsageCardBannerSection     (icon + bold title + dimmer desc;
                       intent default `danger`, web parity).
    FooterSection   -> UsageCardFooterSection     (native flow layout = web `flex-wrap`;
                       in-app routes -> onNavigate closure; external URLs -> SwiftUI
                       `Link`; primary/secondary variants; trailing external-link glyph).
- Intent palette (normal/warn/danger) mapped to the semantic status tokens — the
  native peer of the web intentBarBg / intentBandRing / intentValueText / intentBanner*
  class maps.

------------------------------------------------------------
STATES  (every web-source state renders — no hidden surfaces)
------------------------------------------------------------
The web primitive has exactly these branches (it owns no fetch-tier loading/error/
stale/offline — those live in the CONSUMERS; the native AiUsageCard surface already
implements them, faithfully matching the web architecture):
  - populated (any of budget / bands / details / topLists / banner / footer), across
    all THREE intents (normal / warn / danger)
  - budget over-budget overflow (pct > 100): clamped bar + unclamped a11y percent
  - footer internal route vs external URL, primary vs secondary
  - empty (web `!hasAnything`): friendly muted line, never a blank box
All are rendered (UsageCard.Previews.swift covers Full/normal, Budget/warn,
Budget/danger over 100% + banner, Banner/warn, Footer-only, Empty) and unit/render
tested (UsageCard.Tests.swift).

------------------------------------------------------------
i18n  (P1/S10 — no English literals in Swift)
------------------------------------------------------------
The web primitive holds exactly ONE English literal (the default empty message); every
other string is a prop the consumer localizes. That literal + the native a11y chrome
are promoted to the "UsageCard" table via the UsageCardStrings facade
(NSLocalizedString tableName:"UsageCard", value: fallback):
  usageCard.empty             = "No data to display yet."   (web emptyMessage default)
  usageCard.externalLinkHint  = "Opens in your browser"     (VoiceOver hint)
  usageCard.percent           = "%lld%%"                    (budget a11y value)
No hardcoded English prose remains in the Swift sources.

------------------------------------------------------------
ACCESSIBILITY
------------------------------------------------------------
- Budget bar: one VoiceOver element; label = budget name + headline + caption; value =
  (unclamped) percent.
- Bands / details / top-list rows: combined cell labels via UsageCardAccessibility.
- Banner: combined status element. Footer links: per-link a11y label + external hint.
- Dynamic Type: system fonts (Font.TS) + minimumScaleFactor on tabular values.
- Reduce Motion: the primitive uses NO animations (nothing to gate); decorative icons
  are accessibilityHidden.

------------------------------------------------------------
TELEMETRY  (P1/S11 view.opened)
------------------------------------------------------------
UsageCard.surfaceSlug == "UsageCard". `view.opened` is emitted once on first appear via
the injected UsageCardTelemetry seam (default OSLogUsageCardTelemetry; consent-gated +
redacted in the production adapter). The once-only gate is extracted into the value
type UsageCardOpenEmitter so it is unit-tested with a spy (no view hosting needed).

